                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we calling `exit()` here? As per our existing flow, this API should `throw` so that it is caught by `IbmHandler::performInitialSetup()` where System VPD collection property gets updated properly, and PEL gets logged."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 736,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "as system VPD is not collected, hence we couldn't determine the system type.\nAs this is critical, quiesced the system. system VPD file needs to be available to fix this issue."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 736,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "> system VPD file needs to be available to fix this issue.\n\nCorrect, but if we stop the service, support for tool also goes away in this case.\nGoing forward we plan to keep the service alive even in error cases while logging a critical log in the system."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 736,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "Addressed."
                },
